<title>UK: British Borneo up after Hoare comment.</title>
<headline>British Borneo up after Hoare comment.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in oil exploration group British-Borneo Petroleum Syndicate Plc rose on Friday as analysts at ABN AMRO Hoare Govett rated the stock &quot;undervalued,&quot; dealers said.  </p>
<p>The stock was up 18-1/2p at 10.97-1/2 by 1121 GMT -- close to its record 11.06 stg high reached on January 15, after a surge prompted by bid talk and an upbeat statement on the value of its Morpeth field in the Gulf of Mexico.</p>
<p>Analysts at Hoare Govett were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
